@*
    The approval badge in the admin header, from specification section 3.

    It renders in its empty state because WorkMate.Approvals owns the pending-task count and does
    not exist yet. Showing the badge now, with nothing in it, is the honest version: the chrome is
    in place and the number is visibly absent, rather than a fake count or a gap that nobody
    notices is missing.

    Requesting the shared stylesheet here rather than in a layout means any surface that renders
    WorkMate chrome gets the styling, including the employee front end later.
*@

<style asp-name="workmate-admin" at="Head"></style>

<li class="nav-item workmate-navbar-item">
    <span class="workmate-approval-badge" data-state="none" title="@T["Approvals waiting for you"]">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&#10003;</span>
        <span>@T["Approvals"]</span>
    </span>
</li>
